  "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. q-122092: integrating acceleration gives v(t)=⟨t−t³+5,2t²−t−5⟩, so v(1)=⟨5,−4⟩. q-75221: the variable lower limit gives g′(x)=−f(x), hence g′(2)=2. q-116504: the lower-limit sign and chain rule give −3cos(6x−11). q-94247 and q-131541: standardization gives z=−0.76 and −1.17, yielding 0.2236 and 0.1210 from the supplied tables. q-94327: the standardized interval is (−1.2,−0.19), so its probability is 0.4247−0.1151=0.3096. q-96948 and q-96946: upper-tail probabilities 0.30 and 0.45 correspond to cumulative probabilities 0.70 and 0.55, giving 0.5244 and 0.1257. q-132145: (−1−μ)/5=−0.2 gives μ=0. q-132316: positive interval probability requires μ>0; symmetry gives Φ(6μ/15)=0.7881, hence μ=2 using the table. q-139241 and q-139110: current option 1 in each question is the approximately symmetric, unimodal bell-shaped histogram. Each worked-solution image depicts that histogram with an added normal-curve overlay; the different image paths represent equivalent answers, not a disagreement. Such shape supports possible normality without proving it. q-132712: z=−1.25 gives 0.1056, rounded to 0.11. q-94695: z=0.25 gives 0.5987, rounded to 0.60. q-132856: the central 94% leaves 3% in each tail, so 0.25μ/0.7=1.8808 and μ≈5.27 dollars. q-132852: (1.75−μ)/0.5=−1.8808 gives μ≈2.69 years. Table-based numerical answers use the supplied precision. No submitted-grade evidence was provided; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions.",
